  <section xml:id="ch-12-homework">
    <title>Homework: Adverbials</title>

    <subsection xml:id="ch-12-homework-part1">
      <title>Part 1: Identification and Classification</title>

      <paragraphs>
        <title>Instructions</title>
      </paragraphs>
      <p>For each sentence, identify all adverbials, their form (adverb phrase, prepositional phrase, noun phrase, adverb clause, infinitive phrase, or participial phrase), and their semantic role (time, place, manner, reason, purpose, condition, or concession).</p>

      <paragraphs>
        <title>Example (completed)</title>
      </paragraphs>

      <p><foreign>Yesterday, she worked carefully at the office because she had a deadline.</foreign></p>

      <tabular halign="left">
        <row header="yes" bottom="minor">
          <cell>Adverbial</cell>
          <cell>Form</cell>
          <cell>Semantic Role</cell>
        </row>
        <row><cell><foreign>Yesterday</foreign></cell><cell>NP</cell><cell>time</cell></row>
        <row><cell><foreign>carefully</foreign></cell><cell>AdvP</cell><cell>manner</cell></row>
        <row><cell><foreign>at the office</foreign></cell><cell>PP</cell><cell>place</cell></row>
        <row><cell><foreign>because she had a deadline</foreign></cell><cell>adverb clause</cell><cell>reason</cell></row>
      </tabular>

      <paragraphs>
        <title>Exercises</title>
      </paragraphs>

      <p><em>Exercise 1.</em> <foreign>Last week, the students studied diligently in the library.</foreign></p>
      <ul>
        <li><p>Adverbial 1: __________ Form: __________ Semantic role: __________</p></li>
        <li><p>Adverbial 2: __________ Form: __________ Semantic role: __________</p></li>
        <li><p>Adverbial 3: __________ Form: __________ Semantic role: __________</p></li>
      </ul>

      <p><em>Exercise 2.</em> <foreign>If you need assistance, please call the help desk immediately.</foreign></p>
      <ul>
        <li><p>Adverbial 1: __________ Form: __________ Semantic role: __________</p></li>
        <li><p>Adverbial 2: __________ Form: __________ Semantic role: __________</p></li>
      </ul>

      <p><em>Exercise 3.</em> <foreign>She left early to catch her flight.</foreign></p>
      <ul>
        <li><p>Adverbial 1: __________ Form: __________ Semantic role: __________</p></li>
        <li><p>Adverbial 2: __________ Form: __________ Semantic role: __________</p></li>
      </ul>

    </subsection>

    <subsection xml:id="ch-12-homework-part2">
      <title>Part 2: Adjunct, Disjunct, or Conjunct</title>

      <paragraphs>
        <title>Instructions</title>
      </paragraphs>
      <p>Classify each underlined adverbial as an adjunct (modifies the verb/clause content), disjunct (expresses speaker's attitude), or conjunct (connects sentences).</p>

      <paragraphs>
        <title>Example (completed)</title>
      </paragraphs>

      <p><foreign>Fortunately, the rain stopped before the game.</foreign></p>

      <p><foreign>Fortunately</foreign> — disjunct (expresses the speaker's positive attitude toward the situation)</p>

      <paragraphs>
        <title>Exercises</title>
      </paragraphs>

      <p><em>Exercise 4.</em> <foreign>She answered the questions <em>honestly</em>.</foreign></p>
      <ul>
        <li><p>Classification: __________</p></li>
        <li><p>Explanation: __________</p></li>
      </ul>

      <p><em>Exercise 5.</em> <foreign><em>Honestly</em>, I don't think that's a good idea.</foreign></p>
      <ul>
        <li><p>Classification: __________</p></li>
        <li><p>Explanation: __________</p></li>
      </ul>

      <p><em>Exercise 6.</em> <foreign>The data were inconclusive. <em>Nevertheless</em>, the researchers published their findings.</foreign></p>
      <ul>
        <li><p>Classification: __________</p></li>
        <li><p>Explanation: __________</p></li>
      </ul>

      <p><em>Exercise 7.</em> <foreign>He spoke <em>softly</em> so the children wouldn't wake up.</foreign></p>
      <ul>
        <li><p>Classification: __________</p></li>
        <li><p>Explanation: __________</p></li>
      </ul>

      <p><em>Exercise 8.</em> <foreign>The experiment failed. <em>Therefore</em>, they redesigned the protocol.</foreign></p>
      <ul>
        <li><p>Classification: __________</p></li>
        <li><p>Explanation: __________</p></li>
      </ul>

    </subsection>

    <subsection xml:id="ch-12-homework-part3">
      <title>Part 3: Sentence Completion</title>

      <paragraphs>
        <title>Instructions</title>
      </paragraphs>
      <p>Add the requested type of adverbial to complete each sentence.</p>

      <paragraphs>
        <title>Example (completed)</title>
      </paragraphs>

      <p>Add an adverb clause of condition: __________, you should bring an umbrella.</p>

      <p>Answer: <foreign>If it looks like rain, you should bring an umbrella.</foreign></p>

      <paragraphs>
        <title>Exercises</title>
      </paragraphs>

      <p><em>Exercise 9.</em> Add a prepositional phrase of time: __________, the committee will announce its decision.</p>
      <ul><li><p>Answer: __________</p></li></ul>

      <p><em>Exercise 10.</em> Add an adverb clause of reason: She stayed home __________.</p>
      <ul><li><p>Answer: __________</p></li></ul>

      <p><em>Exercise 11.</em> Add an infinitive phrase of purpose: He went to the store __________.</p>
      <ul><li><p>Answer: __________</p></li></ul>

      <p><em>Exercise 12.</em> Add an adverb clause of concession: __________, we decided to proceed with the project.</p>
      <ul><li><p>Answer: __________</p></li></ul>

      <p><em>Exercise 13.</em> Add a participial phrase functioning as an adverbial: __________, she answered all the questions correctly.</p>
      <ul><li><p>Answer: __________</p></li></ul>

    </subsection>

    <subsection xml:id="ch-12-homework-part4">
      <title>Part 4: Diagramming Adverbials</title>

      <paragraphs>
        <title>Instructions</title>
      </paragraphs>
      <p>For each sentence, complete the labeling table (Role, Phrase, Word, POS), write the bracket notation, and draw a tree diagram. Pay special attention to adverbial elements and their phrase types (ADVP, PP, or clausal).</p>

      <paragraphs>
        <title>Exercises</title>
      </paragraphs>

      <p><em>Exercise 14.</em> <foreign>She spoke very clearly.</foreign></p>
